Fundamentally defeats the topic of reasoning by making a false step on the way there.
基本上通过在过程中犯错来否定推理的主题。

518
00:40:44,495 --> 00:40:45,295
All right.
好吧。

519
00:40:45,575 --> 00:40:46,276
It's interesting.
这很有趣。

520
00:40:47,496 --> 00:40:52,597
Also on this, maybe this prompting misconceptions round of questions.
还有关于这个，或许是关于提示误解的问答环节。

521
00:40:54,137 --> 00:40:55,858
Zach, I know you have strong opinions on this.
扎克，我知道你对此有强烈的看法。

522
00:40:57,045 --> 00:40:58,346
Good grammar, punctuation.
良好的语法，标点符号。

523
00:40:58,746 --> 00:40:59,206
Oh, do I?
哦，我有吗？

524
00:40:59,326 --> 00:41:01,868
Is that necessary in a prompt?
在提示中这是必要的吗？

525
00:41:02,549 --> 00:41:03,109
Do you need it?
你需要它吗？

526
00:41:03,129 --> 00:41:05,390
Do you need to format everything correctly?
你需要把所有东西格式化正确吗？

527
00:41:05,410 --> 00:41:13,255
I usually try to do that because I find it fun, I guess, somehow.
我通常会试着做到这一点，因为我觉得这在某种程度上很有趣。

528
00:41:14,596 --> 00:41:16,337
I don't think you necessarily need to.
我不认为你必须这样做。

529
00:41:16,377 --> 00:41:17,178
I don't think it hurts.
我认为这并没有坏处。

530
00:41:17,618 --> 00:41:24,363
I think it's more that you should have the level of attention to detail that would lead you to doing that naturally.
我觉得更重要的是你应该具备那种细致入微的关注，这会让你自然而然地做到这一点。

531
00:41:25,859 --> 00:41:30,305
If you're just reading over your prompt a lot, you'll probably notice those things and you may as well fix them.
如果你只是多次阅读你的提示，你可能会注意到这些事情，你也可以修正它们。

532
00:41:32,028 --> 00:41:38,156
Like what Amanda was saying, you want to put as much love into the prompt as you do into the code.
就像阿曼达所说的，你希望在提示中投入和代码一样多的爱。

533
00:41:39,689 --> 00:41:50,859
People who write a lot of code have strong opinions about things that I could not care less about, like the number of tabs versus spaces, or opinions about which languages are better.
编写大量代码的人对一些我毫不在意的事情有强烈的看法，比如制表符和空格的数量，或对哪些语言更好的看法。

534
00:41:51,679 --> 00:41:56,163
For me, I have opinionated beliefs about styling of prompts.
对我来说，我对提示的样式有明确的信念。

535
00:41:56,523 --> 00:42:03,489
I can't even say that they're right or wrong, but I think it's probably good to try to acquire those, even if they're arbitrary.
我甚至不能说它们是对还是错，但我认为尝试去获得这些，即使它们是任意的，可能是好的。

536
00:42:04,235 --> 00:42:13,903
I feel personally attacked because I definitely have prompts that are like, I feel like I'm in the opposite end of the spectrum where people will see my prompts and they'll be like, it just has a whole bunch of typos in it.
我感到个人受到攻击，因为我确实有一些提示，我觉得我在光谱的另一端，人们看到我的提示时会说，里面有很多错别字。

537
00:42:13,923 --> 00:42:15,404
And I'm like, yeah, a model knows what I mean.
我想，是的，模型知道我想表达的意思。

